# Test: a DISABLED mcp block with a portless server entry still validates
# VALIDATES: the missing-port guard is gated on `enabled`. ExtractMCPConfig
# returns ok=false for three different configs -- no mcp block, a block that is
# switched off, and a block whose servers do not all name a port -- and only the
# third is a mistake. MCPServersMissingPort answers that one alone.
# PREVENTS: the regression the guard nearly shipped with. Without the enabled
# gate, this config exits 1 and `ze doctor` errors, telling the operator to add a
# port to a service they deliberately turned off. It exits 0 today and must keep
# doing so.
#
# `enabled` is OMITTED rather than written false: the YANG default is false, so
# the omitted leaf is the shape an operator actually leaves behind, and it is the
# one a naive tree walk is most likely to mis-read.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	router-id 10.0.0.1;
	session { asn { local 65533; } }
}
environment {
	mcp {
		server alt {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
